# Tool pins for repository bring-up.
#
# This file is the single definition for every tool version that bring-up installs and
# that is not already pinned by a first-class manifest. It is sourced by
# `scripts/bringup.sh` and `scripts/install_ci_compilers.sh`, and cross-checked against
# `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, `docs/BRINGUP.md`, `docs/RELEASING.md`, and the Rust
# compiler-search constants by `crates/luad-oracle/tests/test_bringup_pins.rs`.
#
# Pins that live elsewhere and are read from their own home, never restated here:
#
#   contributor/release toolchain  rust-toolchain.toml            [toolchain] channel
#   minimum supported Rust         Cargo.toml                     rust-version
#   fuzz nightly and cargo-fuzz    scripts/fuzz_smoke.sh          readonly pinned_*
#   official Lua compiler releases scripts/install_ci_compilers.sh  build_lua arguments
#
# Shell syntax only: every line must be safe to `source` from bash 3.2.

# Dependency-policy tool. CI obtains this exact release through the pinned action tag
# below rather than a `cargo install`, so both values move together.
LUAD_CARGO_DENY_VERSION="0.20.2"
LUAD_CARGO_DENY_ACTION="EmbarkStudios/cargo-deny-action@v2.1.1"

# Release SBOM generator. CI downloads the pinned Linux release asset for this version;
# developer machines install the same version from source.
LUAD_CARGO_CYCLONEDX_VERSION="0.5.9"

# Default install and search directory for the official Lua compilers. It is under the
# user's home because macOS clears /tmp on reboot, which silently disarms every
# differential gate on the next boot.
LUAD_COMPILER_DIR_DEFAULT="${HOME}/.cache/luad/lua-tools/bin"

# Directory searched after the default one. Retained so an existing installation keeps
# working without a reinstall; never the preferred location.
LUAD_LEGACY_COMPILER_DIR="/tmp/lua-tools/bin"

# Build root for the OpenWrt Lua 5.1 LNUM32 authority compiler. It must live beneath
# /tmp because `scripts/build_lua51_openwrt_lnum32.sh` rejects any other location, and
# it matches the root the Linux CI authority gate passes. The compiler is rebuilt by
# the gate on every run; this location only lets the doctor report an existing build.
LUAD_LNUM32_GATE_ROOT="/tmp/gate-authority-lua51-openwrt-lnum32"
